      "sequence_position": 15,
      "problem": "Given that $29≡-16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n\n- $n=5$\n- $n=8$\n- $n=9$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=29-(-16)=45.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $5∣45$ because $45÷5=9,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=5.$\n\n- Note that $8∤45.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=8.$\n\n- Note that $9∣45$ because $45÷9=5,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
